3194139534512 true] [17592186292642 1145 "The tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at the point $a=-4$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a) \\\\  & =f(-4)+{f}^{′}(-4)(x-(-4)) \\\\  & =1+6(x+4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $f(-3.8)$ by evaluating the tangent line approximation at $x=-3.8.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-3.8) & ≈L(-3.8) \\\\  & =1+6(-3.8+4) \\\\  & =1+6(0.2) \\\\  & =1+1.2 \\\\  & =2.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534512 true] [17592186292643 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292644 13194139534512 true] [17592186292643 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534512 true] [17592186292643 1041 "field-1" 13194139534512 true] [17592186292643 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292644 13194139534512 true] [17592186292643 1110 #uuid "af13bb07-56c7-5561-8a85-b2bf26e7eacd" 13194139534512 true] [17592186292644 1034 "2.2" 13194139534512 true] [17592186292644 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534512 true] [17592186292644 1111 #uuid "b132dd43-c97b-5375-8fa6-4ffef4269891" 13194139534512 true] [17592186292645 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292646 13194139534512 true] [17592186292645 1089 "q-346048" 13194139534512 true] [17592186292645 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534512 true] [17592186292645 1100 "An engineer measures the amount of fuel $F$, in liters, remaining in a generator. The following table shows the rate at which fuel is being consumed.\n\n| **$t\\,\\text{(hours)}$** | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{(liters/hour)}$ | $-3.1$ | $-3.5$ | $-4.0$ | $-4.4$ |\n\nAt $t=4,$ the generator contained $62$ liters of fuel. Use the tangent line approximation of $F$ at time $t=4$ to estimate the amount of fuel remaining at $t=4.6.$  Do not round the answer.\n\nThe amount of fuel remaining at $t=4.6$ hours is estimated to be\n{{field-1}}\nliters." 13194139534512 true] [17592186292645 1113 #uuid "2c54b5e6-e3dd-54da-8937-f4265f08e3df" 13194139534512 true] [17592186292645 1145 "The tangent line approximation of $F(t)$ at th